{
  "title": "Numbers and age",
  "note": "Uno becomes un before a masculine noun and una before a feminine one: un libro, una casa. From 31 to 99, numbers are three words joined by y: treinta y dos. Age uses tener, not ser: Tengo veinte años means I am twenty. Cien is exactly 100; from 101 it becomes ciento: ciento uno.",
